Open POSIX Test Suite for RhapsodiOS
====================================

posixtestsuite/ is the Open POSIX Test Suite 1.5.2, unmodified
(posixtestsuite-1.5.2.tar.gz from sourceforge.net/projects/posixtest, sha256
15a2185672127cba851d35ec9d538ff6148defdbb75f99c7e9c50aeba0f94757). It is
licensed under the GPL; see posixtestsuite/COPYING.

The upstream Makefile and timeout helper do not work here (GNU make 3.74,
no pthreads), so the suite is run by ./run with ./ptimeout instead. Tests
are compiled where they run, so the system C compiler must be installed.

Running
-------

    run [-t secs] [-d workdir] [-r root] [-b baseline] [-u] [path ...]

  -t secs      per-test timeout, a positive integer, default 240
  -d dir       where the scratch directory posix.<pid> is made, default /tmp;
               only that subdirectory is removed, at the end
  -r root      suite root, default posixtestsuite/ next to run
  -b baseline  expected results, default baseline next to run
  -u           merge this run's results into the baseline instead of comparing:
               tests not run keep their entry, FLAKY marks are kept
  path         directories under the root to run, default conformance

Each test is compiled with
cc -O -Wall -D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200112L -I<root>/include, linked, and run
under ptimeout with stdin from /dev/null. One line per test goes to stdout
and Report/results:

    POSIX conformance/interfaces/sigaction/1-1 PASS

Compiler, linker and test output is in Report/log/<path>.log.

Results
-------

  BUILD-FAIL   did not compile (often: the interface does not exist here)
  LINK-FAIL    compiled but did not link
  BUILD-ONLY   a compile-only test that compiled
  PASS         exit 0
  FAIL         exit 1
  UNRESOLVED   exit 2, the test could not decide
  UNSUPPORTED  exit 4, an optional feature is missing
  UNTESTED     exit 5
  HUNG         killed at the timeout
  SIGNAL=n     died by signal n
  EXIT=n       any other exit status

Report/summary counts the results, counts build and link failures per API
family, and lists every regression (baseline PASS, now anything else),
improvement (now PASS), other change, and test missing from the baseline.
run exits 1 if there is a regression, 2 if it could not start (no cc, no
baseline, bad -t, a path that does not exist), else 0. A -buildonly test with
a main is also linked to <path>.test, where the shell tests that run it expect it.

Updating the baseline
---------------------

When an API lands or a bug is fixed, the summary shows improvements. Run
`python vm/posix_dev.py baseline` on the host, review the diff of baseline,
and commit it with the kernel it came from in the message. A test seen to
change result between runs on the same kernel is marked FLAKY in baseline
by hand; its changes are never reported.

Not run
-------

posixtestsuite/functional and posixtestsuite/stress are imported but not
run: each has its own Makefile and run.sh, and all except stress/signals
need threads, message queues, semaphores or timers.

Self-test
---------

`make check` runs ptimeout and run against the fixture tests in t/.
